  "quantitative_definitions": {
    "trajectory": "Pooled channel-normalized RMSE of 20 visible q/v channels from the 100 ms origin, excluding the origin, over the stated 1/3/8 s future window. Fixed per-population train RMS scales; formal coarse path h=2.5 ms, qualified against h=1.25 ms.",
    "selection_objective": "Event-equal mean of 0.5 s and 1 s normalized MSE, h=5 ms, complete val=8; this is not RMSE or the formal 3 s/8 s score.",
    "function_errors": "Relative Frobenius/RMS norm error on the preregistered complete val truth-state grid; memory kernel uses the fixed 32 delays from 0.01 to 3 seconds.",
    "amplitudes": "a is the second-harmonic physical coefficient; b=8*raw_b is the physical state-modulated damping coefficient."
  },
  "findings_supported": [
    "All three predeclared populations select the correct function-family support. Absent families are exactly zero and both present amplitudes satisfy the registered 10% relative-error condition.",
    "The independent NumPy truth, matched-parameter causal GN controls and physical/numerical checks pass. The observed recovery failures occur after successful implementation controls.",
    "Null and harmonic selected models pass their train/val trajectory and visible-function gates. Their memory kernels do not meet the registered 5% recovery threshold.",
    "The damping population identifies the added damping family, while conservative-force, memory-kernel and some trajectory gates remain unsatisfied.",
    "All selected train/val trajectories produce correct frozen-rule stability decisions with complete coverage. These classifications do not replace the failed dynamics gates."
  ],
